<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | Overdott Technologies" description="Draft privacy notice for Overdott Technologies Limited website enquiries. Review before publication.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="page-width page-hero-inner"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy · Draft for review</p><h1>Privacy notice</h1><p>This draft explains how website enquiry information may be handled. Review it against actual business practices and applicable Kenyan law before publication.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section page-width article-body" style="max-width:850px"><div class="note-box"><p><strong>Publication note:</strong> This is a starting draft, not legal advice. Confirm the responsible legal entity, lawful basis, retention period, processors, security procedures and data-subject rights process. Seek qualified Kenyan privacy review before launch.</p></div>
    <h2>Information you provide</h2><p>If you send an enquiry, the website collects the information entered, which may include your name, organization, email, phone number, service interest, message, preferred contact method and privacy acknowledgement.</p>
    <h2>How information is used</h2><p>Information may be used to review and respond to your enquiry, communicate about a potential engagement and maintain appropriate business records. Do not send passwords, payment details or unnecessary sensitive personal information through the form.</p>
    <h2>Service providers and transfers</h2><p>The contact form is configured for Netlify Forms when deployed on Netlify. Confirm processing terms, storage locations, retention settings and cross-border transfers before publication. Update this section if other form, hosting, analytics or communications providers are introduced.</p>
    <h2>Retention and security</h2><p>Information should be retained only for a defined business or legal purpose and protected with appropriate administrative and technical measures. The retention period and procedures need confirmation before publication.</p>
    <h2>Your choices and rights</h2><p>Describe the rights and request process that apply under relevant privacy laws, including how to ask about, access, correct or request deletion of personal information. Publish a working privacy contact before launch.</p>
    <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2><p>This initial implementation does not intentionally include analytics or advertising trackers. Review production hosting and future third-party tools; add required consent controls before enabling technologies that need them.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2><p>Replace this placeholder with a verified business privacy contact before publishing: [Privacy contact details to be configured].</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>